+# Feature Specification: Bulk import
+
+**Input**: Public helper `importTasks(list, text)` to import tasks from spreadsheet-like text.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: `text` holds one task per line, as `title;priority;tags`. Blank (whitespace-only) lines are skipped.
+- **FR-002**: An empty priority means `normal`; tags are separated by spaces (any run of whitespace).
+- **FR-003**: Every valid line is added to the list with `list.add`; an invalid line is not.
+- **FR-004**: Returns `{ imported, rejected }`: `imported` is the number of tasks added; `rejected` lists
+  `{ line, reason }` for every line not added, in order, `line` counting from 1 over all lines (blank ones included).
+- **FR-005**: `reason` is the message of the failure (empty title, unknown priority, duplicate title, ...), or
+  says the line has too many `;`-separated fields.
+- **FR-006**: A rejected line changes nothing; the other lines are still imported. Never throws.
+- **FR-007**: Lines end with `\n` or `\r\n`.
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- Priority and tags may be omitted entirely (`Buy milk`, `Buy milk;high`).
+- A line with more than three fields is rejected rather than guessed at.
+- A title already in the list, or earlier in the text, is rejected as a duplicate.
+
+## Plan / Tasks
+
+- [x] `src/domain/import.ts`: `importTasks`, exported with TSDoc; `ImportResult` / `RejectedLine` types.
+- [x] Export from `src/index.ts`.
+- [x] Tests in `test/import.test.ts`.
